fix: restore the Info.plist the version bump had emptied

Bumping to 0.6.2 read the file inside the same expression that truncated
it, so `mac/Resources/Info.plist` was written as empty. A bundle without an
Info.plist cannot be launched as an application: macOS runs the executable
bare, in a defaults domain of its own, where there is no display name, no
LSUIElement and no remembered look or position — the light came up in its
default size at the default spot.

Restored from the previous commit, versioned by reading before writing, and
re-shipped, so bin/DSHLight.app has its identifier and LSUIElement again.
